[[File:Vampyre icon.png|left]]
'''Vyrewatch Sentinels''' are stronger variants of the [[Vyrewatch]], and can be fought after completing the [[Sins of the Father]] quest. They can be found prowling the streets of the upper class areas of [[Darkmeyer]], in search of unruly humans to snack on. The Vyrewatch Sentinels are one of the only monsters that drop the [[blood shard]] (the other being [[venator]]s), although they can also be obtained via pickpocketing the various [[Vyre]] citizens throughout the city.

As with all members of the Vyrewatch, they can only be harmed with the [[Sunspear|Sunspear,]] [[Hallowed flail]], [[Blisterwood sickle]], [[Ivandis flail]], [[Blisterwood flail]], or [[Blisterwood stakes]]. Despite being invulnerable to any damage from weapons like the [[Saradomin godsword]] and [[ancient mace]], special attacks will still heal & restore prayer points as if they had dealt damage. The [[burning claws]] and [[Arkan blade]] special attacks can also apply burn in a similar fashion.

The ability to be assigned vampyres can be purchased for 80 [[Slayer reward point|Slayer reward points]]. Once unlocked, they can be disabled, but players must spend another 80 points to unlock them again.

They can also be killed off task as a low-effort money maker because they can be killed next to an altar and bank.

Before the completion of the quest [[The Blood Moon Rises]], Vyrewatch Sentinels are not [[Tolerance|tolerant]] of the player unless the player is wearing [[vyre noble clothing]]. After completion of the quest, sentinels are no longer aggressive even without wearing vyre clothing. Their aggression can be re-enabled by carrying a [[garlic cocktail]], purchasable from the [[Werewolf (Darkmeyer)|werewolf]] just south of the [[Drakan's medallion]] Darkmeyer teleport.

